    <briefdescription>
<para>Struct template for SFINAE requirements. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1type__traits_1_1requires__" kindref="compound">requires_</ref></computeroutput> struct template is a utility for SFINAE (Substitution Failure Is Not An Error) in template metaprogramming. It is typically used to enable or disable template specialisations and function templates based on compile-time boolean conditions.</para>
<para>When the boolean template parameter is <computeroutput>true</computeroutput>, the specialisation provides a nested <computeroutput>type</computeroutput> alias, which can be used in conjunction with <computeroutput>typename</computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1type__traits_1a1cbbf299a006b4692df250ef2a6fc7c2" kindref="member">requires_t</ref></computeroutput> to enforce requirements in template declarations. </para>
